@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<div class="container py-4" style="max-width: 48rem;">
    <h1 class="display-6 mb-3">Privacy notice</h1>
    <p class="text-muted small mb-4">Last updated: April 2026 &middot; <strong>GLMS</strong> (General Logistics Management System) for TechMove</p>

    <p class="lead">
        This notice describes how GLMS handles information when you use the application. It is intended for
        staff, administrators, and authorised users of the organisation. If you use GLMS, you should read this page.
    </p>

    <hr class="my-4" />

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
        GLMS is an internal web application used to manage client agreements, logistics-related service requests,
        and administrative reporting. The organisation operating the system (for example, TechMove) is the data
        controller for information processed through GLMS, subject to your employer’s policies.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">2. What information GLMS processes</h2>
    <p>Depending on how the system is configured and how you use it, GLMS may process categories such as:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Identity and access:</strong> your Windows or network account name when you sign in (for example, via integrated authentication).</li>
        <li><strong>Business data you enter or maintain:</strong> client names, contact details, regions, contract dates and status, service request descriptions, and amounts stored in South African Rand (ZAR) after any currency conversion performed by the application.</li>
        <li><strong>Operational metadata:</strong> technical identifiers generated by the application (for example, record identifiers and timestamps) as required for normal operation.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">3. How we use information</h2>
    <p>Information is used only to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Provide the features you see in GLMS (for example, creating and reviewing service requests and contracts).</li>
        <li>Enforce access controls so that only authorised users can use the system.</li>
        <li>Maintain integrity of business records (for example, validation rules that prevent certain actions when a contract is not active).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>GLMS is not intended for marketing profiling or unrelated secondary uses.</p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">4. External services</h2>
    <p>
        Some features may contact <strong>third-party services over the internet</strong> to retrieve publicly available
        reference data (for example, currency exchange rates used when capturing amounts). When those features run,
        technical information such as your server’s outbound request may be processed by the third-party provider under
        their own terms and privacy policy. Administrators should ensure use of such services complies with organisational
        and legal requirements.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">5. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
        Like many ASP.NET Core applications, GLMS may use cookies or comparable mechanisms that are <strong>strictly necessary</strong>
        for security and session operation (for example, anti-forgery protection on forms). These are not used for advertising.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">6. Security</h2>
    <p>
        Access to GLMS should be restricted to authorised users. Technical controls (such as authentication and HTTPS in
        production deployments) help protect information in transit. Organisations remain responsible for secure hosting,
        patching, backups, and database access controls.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">7. Retention</h2>
    <p>
        How long data is kept depends on your organisation’s records-management policy and database practices. GLMS itself
        does not automatically delete business records unless such functionality is implemented and configured.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">8. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
        Rights relating to access, correction, or deletion of personal information depend on applicable law and your
        organisation’s HR or data-protection procedures. For requests, contact your <strong>internal administrator</strong>
        or data protection contact rather than the software vendor for this coursework project.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">9. Changes to this notice</h2>
    <p>
        This page may be updated when features or hosting arrangements change. Material changes should be communicated
        internally according to your organisation’s process.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-5 text-muted small">
        This page is provided as application documentation for educational and demonstration purposes and does not replace
        legal advice or a formally approved enterprise privacy policy.
    </p>
</div>
